2|0@TheRedPill^1439636776#cu3sov3:ErasmusOrgasmus$:&gt; Sluttiness is something that can be "ruled in" but is hard to be "ruled out" Correct. It cannot be ruled out completely because AWALT. In other words, all girls have the potential to be sluts due to their biological instincts. However... &gt; but how can you ever be sure that a girl isn't slutty to Chad Thundercocks but acts like a virgin around beta bux? You're asking the right questions. Answer: you CANNOT be sure, ever. Understand that green flags do not offer you any certainty, they merely indicate (a) lower *probability* of slutty behaviour and (b) their past or present will to resist their slutty instincts. This will not be an exhaustive list but some green flags include: - Good, stable family (e.g. good parents who are still together) - In particular, she has a good relationship with her father (hard to test definitively of course but if her father was absent or shitty or if she talks shit about him, it's a RED flag) - Low social media usage (mostly uses it to actually communicate, not posting 300 pictures of her on girls nights out, snapchatting every moment of her day etc) - Able to cook - Decent eating habits (eats cooked meals, relatively balanced diet, not surviving of coke, crisps and takeaways) - Doesn't dress like a slut (obvious but you'd be surprised how many miss this) - Wears minimal makeup - enough to aid her appearance but not enough to make you notice she's wearing makeup as soon as you meet her (I can't really explain this one well, but in my experience girls who look like they applied their makeup by the fistful are sluts, desperate for male attention and have no idea how ridiculous they look) - Decent friends, per your standards (vet her friends and if they seem like decent women as opposed to skanks, it's a good sign) - Doesn't have more male friends than female and doesn't say 'I just get on better with guys' - Is capable of enjoying her own company (doesn't need to be with others 110% of the time) - Has actual, respectable hobbies (reading, outdoor activities like hiking or climbing, drawing = good. If she lists her hobbies as "netflix, food and having fun" nope the fuck out of there.) - Doesn't drink to get drunk (very good sign if she enjoys having a glass or two of wine with you but genuinely sees no value in getting smashed) &gt; As someone who wants to marry a unicorn with low partner count (hoping for 1-2 at most) are there any helpful insights you can share here? My insights are that unicorns do not exist and don't get married. If you ever really believe you've found that girl, why not just limit your commitment to living together as a monogamous couple (assuming common law marriage doesn't apply where you are)? Either tell her that as much as you love her, there are disincentives for you to marry her or else make some shit up about how your favourite granddad got divorce raped by your grandmother and committed suicide and now you hate the institution of marriage.
